    <custom_item>
      type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description     : "1.5 AZLX-23-000125"
      info            : "Amazon Linux 2023 must have GPG signature verification enabled for all software repositories.

GROUP ID: V-273998RULE ID: SV-273998r1119982

Changes to any software components can have significant effects on the overall security of Amazon Linux 2023. This requirement ensures the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor.

All software packages must be signed with a cryptographic key recognized and approved by the organization.

Verifying the authenticity of software prior to installation validates the integrity of the software package received from a vendor. This verifies the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor."
      solution        : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to verify the signature of packages from a repository prior to installation by setting the following option in the \"/etc/yum.repos.d/[your_repo_name].repo\" file:

gpgcheck=1"
      reference       : "800-171|3.4.5,800-171r3|03.04.05,800-53|CM-5(3),800-53r5|CM-14,CAT|I,CCI|CCI-003992,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.4,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.31,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.32,ITSG-33|CM-5(3),LEVEL|1A,NESA|T3.2.3,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NESA|T7.6.3,QCSC-v1|7.2,Rule-ID|SV-273998r1119982_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-000125,Vuln-ID|V-273998"
